<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset='utf-8'>
  <meta name='generator' content='<%= Pluto.generator %> - http://feedreader.github.io/'>

  <title><%= site.title %></title>

  <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="Atom feed" href="atom.xml" />
  <!-- We do one thing well (Atom), we do not advertise RSS.
    -- Note that the RSS feed might not validate in Feed Validator.
    -- If using the RSS feed, read the comment the header of its source.
    -- <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="RSS feed" href="rss20.xml" /> -->
  <link rel="shortcut icon" href="/favicon.ico" />

  <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'css/fontawesome-all' %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'css/blank' %>

  <script src='js/jquery-2.0.3.min.js'></script>
  <script src='js/blank.js'></script>
</head>
<body>

<div id='navwrap'>
<div id='nav'>

  <p><center><a href="https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/credit_and_history.md#aws-open-source-credits"><img src="https://d0.awsstatic.com/logos/powered-by-aws.png" alt="Powered by AWS"></a></center></p>

  <p><center><script type="text/javascript" src="https://cdnjs.buymeacoffee.com/1.0.0/button.prod.min.js" data-name="bmc-button" data-slug="planetMySQLComT" data-color="#FFDD00" data-emoji=""  data-font="Arial" data-text="Buy me a coffee" data-outline-color="#000000" data-font-color="#000000" data-coffee-color="#ffffff" ></script></center></p>

  <p>Last Update:</p>
  <p class='small'><%= site.updated.to_datetime.rfc3339 if site.updated %></p>

  <p><i class="fa-solid fa-square-rss"></i> <%= link_to "Atom feed", "atom.xml" %></p>
  <!-- <p><i class='icon-rss-sign'></i> <%= link_to "RSS 2.0 feed", "rss20.xml" %></p> -->

  <p>Meta:</p>
  <ul class='metas small'>
    <li>Support Planet by following us:
        <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-mastodon"></i>',  "https://fosstodon.org/@Planet_Valkey" %>
        <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-bluesky"></i>',   "https://bsky.app/profile/Planet-Valkey.fosstodon.org.ap.brid.gy" %>
        <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-x-twitter"></i>', "https://x.com/Planet_Valkey" %>
    </li>
    <li>Support Planet by staring us: <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i>', "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/" %></li>
    <li>Financially support us on <%= link_to "Buy me a coffee", "https://buymeacoffee.com/planetmysqlcomt" %></li>
    <li><%= link_to "Abuse procedure", "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/aggregation_and_content_policy.md#abuse-procedure" %></li>
    <li><%= link_to "Aggregation and content policy", "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/aggregation_and_content_policy.md" %></li>
    <li><%= link_to "How to add / remove a feed", "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/aggregation_and_content_policy.md#adding--removing-a-feed" %></li>
    <li>Maintained by <%= link_to "Jean-François Gagné", "https://linktr.ee/jfg.mysql" %></li>
    <li>Sponsored by <%= link_to 'Aiven', "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/credit_and_history.md#aiven-sponsorship" %></li>
    <li>Helped by <%= link_to "many people", "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/credit_and_history.md" %></li>
    <li>Built with the <%= link_to "Pluto Feed Reader", "https://github.com/feedreader" %></li>
    <li>Using <%= link_to "Font Awesome", "http://fontawesome.io" %> v7.3.1</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Planetarium:</p>
  <ul class='planetarium small'>
    <li><%= link_to "Planet for the MySQL Community", "https://planet.oursqlcommunity.org/" %></li>
    <li><%= link_to "Planet MariaDB", "https://mariadb.org/planet/" %></li>
    <li><%= link_to "Planet PostgreSQL", "https://planet.postgresql.org/" %></li>
  </ul>
  <ul class='metas small'>
    <li>(open <%= link_to "issue", "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/issues" %> for adding a data-related Planet)</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Subscriptions:</p>
  <ul class='subscriptions small' >
    <li><hr class='item-separator'></li>
<%
   prefix_old = ""
   site.feeds.each do |feed|

      prefix_new = feed.key[0, feed.key.index("_")]
      separator = prefix_old != prefix_new
      prefix_old = prefix_new

      title = feed.title
      filtered = feed.key.end_with?("_filtered")
      if title.start_with?("_FI_ ")
         title = title[5, title.length-5]
         filtered = true
      elsif title.start_with?("_NF_ ")
         title = title[5, title.length-5]
         filtered = false
      end
%>
    <%= "<li><hr class='item-separator'></li>" if separator %>
    <li>
      <%= link_to '<i class="fa-solid fa-square-rss"></i>', feed.feed_url %>
      <%= link_to title, feed.url %>
      <%= link_to '<small>(<i class="fa-solid fa-filter"></i>)</small>', "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/blob/main/feed_filtering.md" if filtered %>
      <%= ':' if feed.rubygems || feed.meetup || feed.avatar || feed.location || feed.twitter %>
      <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-mastodon"></i>',     "#{feed.rubygems}"               if feed.rubygems  %>
      <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-bluesky"></i>',      "#{feed.meetup}"                 if feed.meetup    %>
      <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-x-twitter"></i>',    "https://x.com/#{feed.twitter}"  if feed.twitter   %>
      <%= link_to '<i class="fa-brands fa-linkedin-in"></i>',  "#{feed.avatar}"                 if feed.avatar    %>
      <%= link_to '<i class="fa-solid  fa-link"></i>',         "#{feed.location}"               if feed.location  %>
    </li>
<% end %>

    <li><hr class='item-separator'></li>
    <li><hr class='item-separator'></li>
   </ul>
</div>
</div>

<div id='opts'>
  <div style='width: 100%; text-align: right;'>
   <img src='image/view-headlines.png' id='show-headlines' title='Show Headlines Only' width='24' height='24'>
   <img src='image/view-snippets.png'  id='show-snippets'  title='Show Snippets'       width='24' height='24'>
  </div>
</div>

<h1 style='margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px'><%= site.title %></h1>
<h3 style='margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px'>A blog / news aggregator (Planet) for the <%= link_to "Valkey", "https://valkey.io/" %> Community / Ecosystem</h3>

<p>This is a demo of what a Blog / News Aggregator (Planet) for the Valkey Community / Ecosystem would look like.</p>

<p>(will be replaced by <%= link_to "Planet Valkey", "https://planet.valkey.io/" %>)
<br>(update your bookmarks, because soon, this website will stop working)
<br>(the reason for replacement is that the initial URL is on the wrong domain, and new name and URL are better)
<br>(before this website stops working, announcments will be made, and service will slowly degrade to nudge migration)
<br>(announcments will include posts in the feed to reach people not checking the website)
<br>(degradations will include removing subscriptions, and reducing refresh frequency)
<br>(feel free to follow progress and share feedback in this <%= link_to "GitHub Issue", "https://github.com/valkey-io/planet/issues/23" %>)</p>

<div id="articles">
<%
   items = site.items.latest.limit(100)
   ItemCursor.new( items ).each do |item, new_date, new_feed|
      title = item.feed.title
      if title.start_with?("_FI_ ")
         title = title[5, title.length-5]
      elsif title.start_with?("_NF_ ")
         title = title[5, title.length-5]
      end
%>
<% if new_date %>
  <h2 class='new-date'><%= item.updated.strftime('%A, %d. %B %Y') %></h2>
<% else %>
  <hr class='item-separator'>
<% end %>
  <article class='item'>
    <h3 class='item-title'>
      <i class='fa-solid fa-caret-down  item-collapse item-close item-opened'></i>
      <i class='fa-solid fa-caret-right item-expand   item-open  item-closed'></i>
      <%= link_to item.title, item.url %>
      <sup><small>(from <%= link_to title, item.feed.url %>)</small></sup>
    </h3>
    <div class='item-body'>
      <div class='item-snippet'>
<% if item.summary %>
        <%= textify( item.summary )[0..400] %>
<% elsif item.content %>
        <%= textify( item.content )[0..400] %>
<% else %>
        -/-
<% end %>
        [...]
      </div>
      <div class='item-footer'>
        Published <%= item.published.strftime('%A, %d. %B %Y %H:%M') %> &bull;
                  <%= time_ago_in_words( item.published ) %>
<% if item.updated != item.published %>
        &vert; Updated <%= item.updated.strftime('%A, %d. %B %Y %H:%M') %> &bull;
                <%= time_ago_in_words( item.updated ) %>
<% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
<% end %>
<hr class='item-separator'>
</div>
</body>
</html>
